ions:**\\n   - Ensure the function handles an empty `strings` list by returning an empty list.\\n   - Ensure the function handles an empty `prefix` by returning the original `strings` list.\\n   - Ensure the function correctly filters strings based on the exact prefix match.\\n\\n4. **Edge Cases:**\\n   - Test with an empty `strings` list.\\n   - Test with an empty `prefix`.\\n   - Test with strings of varying lengths.\\n   - Test with strings that partially match the prefix.\\n\\n5. **Complexity:**\\n   - Time: O(n * m), where n is the number of strings and m is the average length of the strings.\\n   - Space: O(k), where k is the number of strings starting with the prefix.\\n\\nBy following this checklist, the coder can ensure a correct and efficient implementation of the `filter_by_prefix` function."}'}]
